      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The INVEST (INternational VErapamil SR-Trandolapril) study, a very large international study of hypertensive patients, has shown that patients with type 2 diabetes and coronary artery disease do not benefit from tightening systolic blood pressure levels to below 130 mmHg, and this may in some cases be harmful."},
